Tested 2026-10-09 on NetBSD-current 11.99.9/amd64 with samba-4.24.7:
- An authenticated SMB2/3 share on a QNAP NAS: list, read, create and
  write all work.
- A guest share on a local smbd: list, read, create and mkdir work.
  Writing data fails with EACCES, and smbclient(1) is denied the same
  way, so this is the server's guest permissions, not smbnetfs.

Open:
- umount(8) of a live mount hangs in "puffsrpl" waiting for the daemon,
  and concurrent mount(8) calls then block in "fstchg".  Killing the
  daemon with SIGKILL releases the mount.  Find out whether refuse/puffs
  or smbnetfs fails to handle the unmount request.
- df(1) reports 0 blocks unless -o free_space_size=N is given.
- Not yet tested on netbsd-10 or on other architectures.
